		{"id":"5102b0c404df57a6","type":"text","text":"# EnergyLab Nordhavn\n\nhttp://www.energylabnordhavn.com/\n\nInteresting publications that came out of this experiment\n\n- Modelling energy flexibility of low energy buildings utilising thermal mass\n- Intelligent scheduling of grid connected heat pump in a Danish Detached House\n- Performance of ultra low temperature district heating systems with utility plant and booster heat pumps\n- Potential Energy flexibility for a hot water based heating system in smart buildings via economic MPC\n- Quantifying the demand flexibility of power-to-heat and thermal energy storage in the control of building heat systems\n- Demand side management in urban district heating networks\n- Combined provision of primary frequency regulation from V2G EVs and community scale heat pumps","x":-660,"y":555,"width":340,"height":85,"color":"2"},
